# The records live in their own repository.
#
# This one is the MCP tooling: harness, adapters, CLI, server. The knowledge it
# produces -- runs, plans, reports, verdicts, the ancestry between them -- and
# the task packages whose runs they are accumulate in the tasks repository
# instead, pointed at by $RLMCP_RECORDS. Carrying them here meant every
# experiment dirtied the tool's history, mostly with training logs and video.
# An in-tree ./records remains the scratch default for a quick local try.
#
# Both forms on purpose: `/records/` matches a real directory, and a bare
# `/records` also matches a symlink pointing at the tasks checkout -- which is
# what you end up with when you want the rendered records page to be served
# from this directory. git treats that symlink as a file, so the
# trailing-slash form alone lets it through.
#
# Both are anchored to the repository root. Unanchored, `records/` also matches
# `rlmcp/records/` -- the package that holds the record schema and the viewer --
# so every *new* file added there was silently ignored while the ones already
# tracked kept showing up, which is the most confusing shape this mistake has.
/records/
/records

# A play or train session writes here when nobody said where. Same reasoning as
# `/records` above, and the same anchoring: a session is a run artifact, not the
# tool. Four of these files reached a pull request before this line existed.
/rlmcp_session/
/rlmcp_session

# A run's raw log is not its record, and is regenerable by re-running.
*.log
MUJOCO_LOG.TXT

# Ad-hoc uv runs resolve fresh from pyproject; no lockfile is managed
uv.lock

# Agent worktrees of this repository, created under .claude/. They are
# checkouts, not content: committing one embeds a git repo inside this one.
.claude/worktrees/
